 the evening of her life she longed to give up her material body and to attain salvation. At this juncture nārada told her that salvation was not for unmarried women. She, therefore, gave half the power of her penance to a young man called śṛṅgavān and lived as his wife for one single night. She thus attained salvation (śalya Parva, Chapter 52).", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["kuNigarga", "kuṇigarga", "కుణిగర్గ", "ಕುಣಿಗರ್ಗ"], "synonyms_slp1": ["kuNigarga", "kuṇigarga", "కుణిగర్గ", "ಕುಣಿಗರ್ಗ"]}], "kuRinda": [{"id": "kuRinda", "headword": "कुणिन्द", "headword_slp1": "kuRinda", "fold": "kuRinda", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "purana-encyclopedia", "senses": [{"gloss": "कुणिन्द\n\nKUṆINDA . A noble brahmin. He presented a divine conch to yudhiṣṭhira at his rājasūya yajña. (Śabhā Parva, Chapter 51, Southern text).", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["kuNinda", "kuṇinda", "కుణిన్ద", "ಕುಣಿನ್ದ"], "synonyms_slp1": ["kuNinda", "kuṇinda", "కుణిన్ద", "ಕುಣಿನ್ದ"]}]}